 "conclusion": "Worker service-speed differences existed before frontend routing. The startup readiness race is real and now gated; its correlation with speed groups is not unique causal proof. Old telemetry cannot uniquely attribute total variance to routing, kernels, hardware, or warmup.",
 "limitations": [
  "Requests store planned arrival, not actual wake/send timestamp. client_queue_seconds measures semaphore waiting only. Proxy clocks cannot prove actual request send/completion times.",
  "Client (latency-ttft)/output_tokens approximates online frontend TPOT; exact frontend feedback timestamps and frame timing were not saved.",
  "Worker logs have second precision and no per-request identifiers; request-to-batch mapping and exact MPQ group/allocator timing cannot be reconstructed.",
  "Only final migration/replication counts were saved; per-event movement/key/cost vectors are absent. No causal attribution of 58 vs 110 migrations is proven.",
  "Prefill new-token log totals quantify logged work, not an attributed eviction/retraction recomputation count. Active token usage excludes evictable capacity.",
  "Input hash and planned arrivals are identical, but 124 output hashes differ, and dynamic batching/greedy numerical reproducibility is not guaranteed.",
  "No continuous GPU utilization, SM/memory clocks, power, temperature, throttling, CPU load, affinity, NUMA placement, or per-kernel/collective timings were archived.",
  "Same recorded launch/environment/server_info does not prove identical device/CPU runtime state or performance.",
  "Existing cache mtimes are retrospective metadata, not an immutable before/after trace; absence of writes does not exclude other process-local/lazy initialization.",
  "512/printed input-throughput reconstructs adjacent prefill-report wall-time gaps (rounded throughput), not individual GPU kernel durations. First interval after idle/flush is excluded; last 466-token chunk of profile3 is excluded.",
  "Warmup overlap exactly matches observed slow/fast groups in these six worker sessions, but no controlled intervention proves that overlap caused persistent speed differences.",
  "Only two Preble repetitions; cannot apportion the full end-to-end variance or prove a unique hardware/backend cause.",
  "The legitimate EOS finish explains the 13 output-token difference, but full generated text/tokens were not archived, so its numerical cause cannot be recovered.",
  "Ready marker guarantees successful builtin HTTP warmup and prior local TP initialization, not an additional post-warmup dist.barrier.",
  "Gate log hashes cover the immutable prefix through completed_line_end_byte; running full logs are intentionally not hashed."
 ],
